restrictions: []
side_effects: "Vulnerabilities/Penalties: none, as printed. Player characters start at first or second level of experience; NPCs average 1D4+2. A True Inca on a mission for the Empire is clothed, fed and equipped at no cost in any dwelling or province of the Empire."
extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts World Book 9: South America 2 printed 20-23 (cache p020-p023,
    page_offset 0; p022 is a full-page illustration). The stat block is on
    printed 21 and was read off a 200 dpi render as well as the OCR; the
    two agree. The weapons, armor and money run onto printed 23.
  - xp_table: the True Inca ladder, printed 192, lower bounds, as briefed.
  - men_of_arms false: a race (R.C.C.) that states mdc_base and no S.D.C.
    or hit points.
  - PATRON DEITY: stored as ONE choose-1 special ability group, one ability
    per patron (Viracocha, Inti, Pachamama, Illapa), each carrying its own
    bonuses, psionics and magic blocks. NOT variants: variants cannot
    override magic or psionics (VARIANT_OVERRIDES, js/parser.js), and a
    variant''s bonuses would replace the class''s rather than add to them.
    The class itself states no psionics or magic block, so the chosen
    patron''s blocks arrive whole.
  - M.D.C.: P.E. x8, plus the P.E. number per additional level, stored as
    printed. The per-level increment is a fixed number, not dice; on
    2026-09-25 the level-up proposal grew only dice terms
    (perLevelDiceOf), so the increment is added by hand at each level.
    The patron M.D.C. bonus (+1D6x10 Viracocha, +10 Inti) is a pool bonus
    on the ability. S.D.C. bonuses from physical skills counting as M.D.C.
    is a natural_abilities line, not stored as a number.
  - P.P.E.: the book gives 2D6x10 + P.E., +15 per level for a
    practitioner of magic and 1D4x10 otherwise. Three of the four patrons
    (Viracocha, Pachamama, Illapa) grant spells, so ppe_base holds the
    practitioner formula. JUDGEMENT CALL: an Inti Inca, who has no spells,
    should have 1D4x10; ability grants carry no pool base, so this is
    stated in the Inti ability text for the player/GM to correct. The +15
    per level is a fixed increment, handled as the M.D.C. one is.
  - I.S.P.: 2D4x10 + M.E., +2D6 per level, for every True Inca with
    psionics, stored on each patron''s psionics block.
  - PSIONIC TIER is not printed. Viracocha, Pachamama and Illapa are
    stored major (4, 10 and 5 powers plus per-level gains); Inti, whose
    only psychic powers are two Burster abilities, is stored minor with
    no picks. Illapa''s Hydrokinesis is a Super catalog power, granted by
    name beside four picks from Sensitive, Healing and Physical ("the
    three non-super categories"). Inti''s Extinguish Flame and Sense Fire
    have no psionic_powers rows (Burster pyrokinetic abilities) and are
    ability text.
  - MAGIC: Viracocha picks 4 each from spell levels 1, 2, 3 (general
    invocations) and 2 per level up to his own level. Pachamama picks 3
    each from earth warlock levels 1-3 and 1 per level; Illapa 3 each from
    water warlock levels 1-3 and 2 per level. The warlock starting groups
    are inline per-level lists, the per-level picks a 14-entry schedule
    (levels 2-15) drawing from the full EARTH (62) or WATER (52) warlock
    list capped at the character''s level (F61). Pachamama''s Heal Wounds
    and psionic Healing Touch are granted by name, beside her picks.
  - "Magic Powers: plus add one attack/action per melee" is stored as
    combat.attacks 1 on the three spell-casting patrons only.
  - Bonuses: +1D4 initiative, +1 strike/parry/dodge, +2 save vs magic
    (spell_magic), +6 vs horror factor, all unconditional. Horror Factor
    10 when revealed is the top-level horror_factor phrase.
  - Inti''s flight, nimbus, energy field and sun-bolts; Illapa''s flight,
    Summon Storm 3/day and lightning; Pachamama''s six-a-day healing touch;
    Viracocha''s exorcism 60% +3% and immunities: ability text. No
    trackable_resources: a class-level resource cannot depend on the
    patron chosen, so the daily uses are in the text.
  - SKILLS: Dragonese/Elven 98% -> Language: Dragonese 98; Quechua and
    Spanish 98; one language of choice +20 as a Language: Other pick;
    Demon and Monster Lore -> Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+20 = 45; Basic
    Math -> Mathematics: Basic 45+10 = 55; Wilderness Survival 30+15 =
    45; two W.P.s of choice. Hand to Hand: Expert changes to Martial Arts
    for one other skill (costs martial_arts 1).
  - This R.C.C. prints its own related (8, +2 at levels 3, 7, 10, 14) and
    secondary (5) skills, so both are stored. Electrical and Military are
    None and omitted. Pilot except robots and power armor uses the same
    exclusion list as anti-monster. Horsemanship and Cowboy are not on the
    printed list and are not granted.
  - EQUIPMENT: magic club, enchanted spear and enchanted cloth armor (90
    M.D.C.) are this book''s catalog rows. "One energy weapon" is a choice
    from the Empire''s four small arms; "two normal archaic weapons" a
    choice from a catalog set. Survival gear: backpack, fishing line and
    hooks, rope, one week''s rations (food-rations), a holistic first-aid
    kit (first-aid-kit, noted), hammock, tent. Money 1D4x1000 credits in
    coins.
  - The holy items at levels 3, 5, 6 and 9 depend on continued service
    and a choice; they are level_progression text, not equipment.
  - Alliances (Inca warriors, line makers, rune warriors, other
    pantheons of light, cosmo-knights, undead slayers, cyber-knights) are
    GM notes.
---

## Lore

True Incas are demigods of the Pantheon of the Sun, the Inca gods led by
Viracocha. They founded the Inca Empire about eight centuries before the
Rifts, left Earth soon after, and handed the realm to human believers. They
may be lesser descendants of the gods or favoured servants raised up as a
reward, and like other demigods they live for ages.

They are tall and athletic, a little fairer than most Andean people, and it
was this that let the Spanish be mistaken for returning demigods. Each has a
patron god whose nature shapes their powers: a Viracocha Inca commands
spirits and magic, an Inti Inca light and fire. They dress in bright tunics
and capes and wear large ornate earrings.

Most serve the Pantheon loyally as protectors, judges and commanders of the
Empire, and as its messengers, troubleshooters and scouts, often against the
Arkhons, whose Spectral Hunters are sent to kill them. A few have broken
away; some are renegades and warlords, while others simply wander the
Megaverse as heroes.

## GM Notes

Alignment: any, but most are good or unprincipled. They work closely with the
Inca Warriors, Line Makers and Rune Warriors, and with demigods and godlings of
other pantheons of light, cosmo-knights, undead slayers and cyber-knights. They
travel alone, with mortals, or in groups rarely larger than four or five, and
can usually reach their patron god when it matters.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'true-inca');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'true-inca';

